@* ProductDetail.razor — Phase 3.2 (rewritten for staff edit + customer view)

   Product detail page at route `/Products/{Id:guid}`. Reached from the
   Products grid by clicking a product card. ALL authenticated users can
   view this page — the role determines what they see + can do.

   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   TWO VIEWS BASED ON ROLE
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

   CUSTOMER VIEW (Customer role, and anyone not in Admin/Manager/Employee):
     - Breadcrumb: Products → [Category / Sub / SubSub] → [Product Name]
     - Product picture (or placeholder)
     - Product name (read-only)
     - Price (read-only)
     - Description (read-only)
     - Category hierarchy label (Category › SubCategory › SubSubCategory)
     - Quantity selector (1 to MyPurchaseLimit, if a limit applies)
     - Add to Cart button
     - NO stock number is shown.
     - NO groups, NO purchase limits, NO internal audit details.

   STAFF VIEW (Admin, Manager, Employee — authorized by [RequireRoles]
   on the command handlers themselves; the page just checks role via
   AuthenticationStateProvider to decide what UI to render):
     Everything in the customer view EXCEPT the staff sees additional
     edit affordances below the read-only display:
       1. Change Photo button → opens the same dropzone + preview card UI
          used on CreateProduct.razor. Same JPEG/PNG/WebP + 5 MB rules.
          On save: (a) upload new file via IFileStorage.SaveAsync,
                   (b) delete the OLD file via IFileStorage.DeleteAsync
                       (hard delete — orphaned images are cleaned up),
                   (c) dispatch UpdateProductDetailsCommand with the new
                       PictureUrl + the existing Name/Description/Price
                       (UpdateProductDetails is the only command that
                       can change PictureUrl).
       2. Edit Name + Description → two text inputs + Save button.
          Dispatches UpdateProductDetailsCommand with the new values
          (PictureUrl is passed as the existing value — unchanged).
       3. Per-group purchase limits editor:
          - Loads ALL existing customer groups via GetAllCustomerGroupsQuery
            (every existing group must have a limit OR be explicitly
            set to "no limit" by leaving the field empty + clicking
            "Remove limit").
          - For each existing limit on this product, shows a row with
            the group name (read-only) + the current limit (editable
            RadzenNumeric) + a Save button per row.
          - For each existing group that has NO limit set on this
            product, shows a row with the group name + an empty limit
            input + a "Set limit" button.
          - "Add custom group" button below the list lets staff set a
            limit for a group name that doesn't have any users yet
            (forward-looking). Mirrors CreateProduct's pattern.

   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   ROLE CHECK
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Uses AuthenticationStateProvider (NOT ICurrentUserService.IsInRole)
   because in interactive Blazor Server mode, ICurrentUserService reads
   from IHttpContextAccessor.HttpContext which is null over the SignalR
   circuit. Same pattern as Sales.razor + SaleDetail.razor.

   The backend command handlers ALSO enforce [RequireRoles] as
   defense-in-depth — even if a non-staff user could see the buttons,
   the handler would reject the dispatch.

   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   IMAGE UPLOAD FLOW (mirrors CreateProduct.razor — same rules)
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   - Dropzone + InputFile with accept="image/jpeg,image/png,image/webp".
   - Validates content type + 5 MB max size client-side.
   - Buffers the bytes IMMEDIATELY in OnInputFileChange (not at submit
     time) to avoid the JSException that occurs when the JS-side
     _blazorFilesById registry is cleared by Hot Reload / circuit
     reconnect / runtime housekeeping.
   - Generates a downscaled data: URL preview (400×400 max) via
     IBrowserFile.RequestImageFileAsync.
   - On "Save photo": stream bytes to IFileStorage.SaveAsync → get URL,
     then IFileStorage.DeleteAsync(oldPictureUrl) to hard-delete the
     previous file, then dispatch UpdateProductDetailsCommand with
     new PictureUrl + existing Name/Description/Price.

   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   LOCALIZATION
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   All user-visible strings via IStringLocalizer<ProductDetail> (Loc).
   Keys in ProductDetail.fa-IR.resx + ProductDetail.en-US.resx.
   RTL handled at the <html dir> level by MainLayout.

   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   TIMEZONE (Tehran, not UTC)
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   No timestamps displayed on this page currently. If timestamps are
   added in the future, use the same inline +3:30 offset arithmetic
   used in Sales.razor / SaleDetail.razor. Server runs in UTC; using
   .LocalDateTime would show UTC times instead of Tehran times.

   ANTIFORGERY:
     Not needed — no EditForm. All buttons are regular RadzenButtons
     with async Click handlers that dispatch commands via Wolverine.
     The Blazor circuit's anti-forgery token is established at circuit
     start. No form POST happens.

   ROUTE PARAMETER:
     `Id` is a Guid bound from the URL via [Parameter]. The @page
     constraint `{Id:guid}` validates the URL segment is parseable as
     a Guid before this component even loads — a malformed URL gets a
     404 from the router, not a runtime exception here. *@

@page "/Products/{Id:guid}"
@attribute [Authorize]
@using System.Globalization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Authorization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Forms
@using Wolverine
@using TakOne.Application.Common.Authorization
@using TakOne.Application.Common.Interfaces
@using TakOne.Application.Products.DTOs
@using TakOne.Application.Products.Queries.GetProductById
@using TakOne.Application.Products.Commands.UpdateProductDetails
@using TakOne.Application.Products.Commands.UpdateProductCategory
@using TakOne.Application.Products.Commands.SetProductPurchaseLimit
@using TakOne.Application.Products.Commands.RemoveProductPurchaseLimit
@using TakOne.Application.Products.Commands.SetProductStock
@using TakOne.Application.Categories.DTOs
@using TakOne.Application.Categories.Queries.GetCategoryByIdWithHierarchy
@using TakOne.Application.Categories.Queries.GetActiveCategories
@using TakOne.Application.Customers.Queries.GetAllCustomerGroups
@using TakOne.Application.Customers.DTOs
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.Common
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.DTOs
@using TakOne.WebUI.Services
@inject IMessageBus MessageBus
@inject AuthenticationStateProvider AuthStateProvider
@inject NavigationManager Navigation
@inject IStringLocalizer<ProductDetail> Loc
@inject ToastService Toast
@inject ErrorDisplayService ErrorDisplay
@inject IFileStorage FileStorage

<PageTitle>@(_product is null ? Loc["PageTitle"] : $"{_product.Name} — TakOne")</PageTitle>

<HeadContent>
    <style>
            /* Layout — 12-col grid on desktop/tablet, stacks on mobile */
            .detail-grid {
                display: grid;
                grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 7fr);
                gap: 2rem;
                align-items: start;
            }

            @@media (max-width: 768px) {
                .detail-grid {
                    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
                    gap: 1.25rem;
                }
            }

            /* Picture — square aspect ratio, placeholder-friendly. */
            .detail-picture {
                position: relative;
                aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                justify-content: center;
                background: var(--rz-base-background-color);
                border: 1px solid var(--rz-base-border-color);
                border-radius: var(--rz-border-radius);
                overflow: hidden;
                max-width: 480px;
            }

                .detail-picture img {
                    width: 100%;
                    height: 100%;
                    object-fit: contain;
                }

                .detail-picture .rz-icon {
                    font-size: 8rem;
                    color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                }

            /* Left-column wrapper — holds the picture AND the staff-only
                                                                       photo-editor card (when open) stacked vertically. Putting
                                                                       both inside one wrapper (instead of leaving the photo
                                                                       editor as a sibling of .detail-picture inside the grid)
                                                                       keeps them in the SAME grid cell, so the editor appears
                                                                       flush against the bottom of the picture with no gap
                                                                       (the grid's align-items: start would otherwise push the
                                                                       editor down to row 2, leaving a vertical gap equal to
                                                                       the difference between the picture's height and the
                                                                       info column's height).

                                                                       Max-width matches .detail-picture so the editor card
                                                                       doesn't sprawl wider than the picture on wide screens. */
            .detail-picture-column {
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                gap: 1rem;
                max-width: 480px;
                width: 100%;
            }

            /* "Change photo" button — overlaid on the picture bottom-right
                                                                           corner. Only shown to staff. Uses RadzenButton underneath
                                                                           but is positioned via a wrapper. */
            .change-photo-overlay {
                position: absolute;
                inset-inline-end: 0.5rem;
                bottom: 0.5rem;
            }

            /* Purchase panel — the right column */
            .detail-info {
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                gap: 1rem;
            }

            .detail-name {
                font-size: 1.6rem;
                font-weight: 700;
                margin: 0;
                line-height: 1.2;
            }

            .detail-price {
                font-size: 1.75rem;
                font-weight: 700;
                color: var(--rz-primary);
                line-height: 1;
            }

            .detail-description {
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                line-height: 1.6;
                white-space: pre-wrap; /* preserves newlines in description */
            }

            /* Category hierarchy chip — small inline label */
            .category-hierarchy {
                display: flex;
                flex-wrap: wrap;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.4rem;
                font-size: 0.875rem;
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
            }

                .category-hierarchy .crumb-sep {
                    opacity: 0.5;
                }

            /* Breadcrumb */
            .breadcrumb {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.4rem;
                font-size: 0.85rem;
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
                flex-wrap: wrap;
            }

                .breadcrumb a {
                    color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                    text-decoration: none;
                }

                    .breadcrumb a:hover {
                        color: var(--rz-primary);
                        text-decoration: underline;
                    }

                .breadcrumb .crumb-current {
                    color: var(--rz-text-primary-color);
                    font-weight: 600;
                }

                .breadcrumb .crumb-sep {
                    opacity: 0.5;
                }

            /* ── STAFF EDIT SECTION ────────────────────────────────────── */
            .staff-section {
                border-top: 1px dashed var(--rz-base-border-color);
                padding-top: 1.5rem;
                margin-top: 1.5rem;
            }

            .staff-section-title {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.5rem;
                font-weight: 600;
                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
            }

            .edit-row {
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                gap: 0.5rem;
                margin-bottom: 1rem;
            }

            .edit-actions {
                display: flex;
                gap: 0.5rem;
                justify-content: flex-end;
            }

            /* Picture upload section — dropzone + preview card.
                                                                           Mirrors CreateProduct.razor's picture-dropzone styles so the
                                                                           two pages share a consistent upload UI. */
            .upload-section {
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                gap: 0.75rem;
            }

            .field-label {
                display: block;
                font-size: 0.875rem;
                font-weight: 500;
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
            }

            .picture-dropzone {
                display: block;
                cursor: pointer;
                border: 2px dashed var(--rz-border-color);
                border-radius: 8px;
                background: var(--rz-base-background-color);
                padding: 2rem 1.5rem;
                text-align: center;
                transition: border-color 0.15s ease, background-color 0.15s ease;
            }

                .picture-dropzone:hover {
                    border-color: var(--rz-primary);
                    background-color: var(--rz-primary-lighter, rgba(0, 100, 250, 0.04));
                }

                .picture-dropzone:focus-within {
                    border-color: var(--rz-primary);
                    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(0, 100, 250, 0.15);
                    outline: none;
                }

            .picture-dropzone-input {
                position: absolute;
                width: 1px;
                height: 1px;
                padding: 0;
                margin: -1px;
                overflow: hidden;
                clip: rect(0, 0, 0, 0);
                white-space: nowrap;
                border: 0;
            }

            .picture-dropzone-body {
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.75rem;
                pointer-events: none;
            }

            .picture-dropzone-text {
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                gap: 0.25rem;
            }

            .picture-dropzone-title {
                font-weight: 600;
                color: var(--rz-text-color);
                font-size: 0.95rem;
            }

            .picture-dropzone-hint {
                font-size: 0.8rem;
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
            }

            .upload-card {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 1rem;
                padding: 1rem;
                border: 1px solid var(--rz-border-color);
                border-radius: 8px;
                background: var(--rz-base-background-color);
            }

            .upload-preview {
                width: 96px;
                height: 96px;
                object-fit: cover;
                border-radius: 6px;
                border: 1px solid var(--rz-border-color);
                flex-shrink: 0;
            }

            .upload-preview-placeholder {
                width: 96px;
                height: 96px;
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                justify-content: center;
                border-radius: 6px;
                border: 1px dashed var(--rz-border-color);
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                font-size: 2rem;
                flex-shrink: 0;
            }

            .upload-info {
                flex: 1 1 auto;
                min-width: 0;
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                gap: 0.25rem;
            }

                .upload-info .file-name {
                    font-weight: 500;
                    overflow: hidden;
                    text-overflow: ellipsis;
                    white-space: nowrap;
                    color: var(--rz-text-color);
                }

                .upload-info .file-size {
                    color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                    font-size: 0.85rem;
                }

            /* Purchase-limits editor — same row shape as CreateProduct */
            .limit-row {
                display: flex;
                align-items: end;
                gap: 0.5rem;
                flex-wrap: wrap;
                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
            }

                .limit-row > * {
                    flex: 0 0 auto;
                }

            /* Category editor — three dropdowns in a row, mirroring
                                                                       CreateProduct.razor's .category-row. Wraps on narrow
                                                                       screens (each dropdown takes full width below 768px). */
            .category-row {
                display: grid;
                grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
                gap: 0.75rem;
            }

            @@media (max-width: 768px) {
                .category-row {
                    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
                }
            }

            /* Back button row — mirrors the detail-grid columns so the
                                                               button stays aligned with the START of the info column
                                                               (right above the breadcrumb) in both LTR and RTL modes.
                                                               The button cell uses flex + justify-content: flex-start so
                                                               the button sizes to its content instead of stretching to
                                                               the full cell width. */
            .back-button-row {
                display: grid;
                grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 7fr);
                gap: 2rem;
            }

            .back-button-cell {
                display: flex;
                justify-content: flex-start;
            }

            @@media (max-width: 768px) {
                .back-button-row {
                    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
                }

                .back-button-spacer {
                    display: none;
                }
            }
    </style>
</HeadContent>

<RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Gap="1rem">
    @* ── Back button ──
       Role-aware: staff (Admin/Manager/Employee) see "Back to manage products"
       and go to /Admin/Products; everyone else sees "Back to catalog" and
       goes to /Products. Wrapped in a grid that mirrors the detail-grid
       layout (5fr picture | 7fr info) so the button stays aligned with the
       START of the info column — right above the breadcrumb text — in both
       LTR and RTL modes. The button itself is sized to its content
       (justify-content: flex-start in .back-button-cell prevents it from
       stretching to the cell width). *@
    <div class="back-button-row">
        <div class="back-button-spacer" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="back-button-cell">
            <RadzenButton Text="@(_canEdit ? Loc["BackToManageProducts"] : Loc["BackToCatalog"])"
                          Icon="arrow_back"
                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Secondary"
                          Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                          Click="@GoBackAsync" />
        </div>
    </div>

    @* ── Loading state ── *@
    @if (_isLoading)
    {
        <RadzenCard>
            <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.75rem">
                <RadzenProgressBarCircular ShowValue="false" Mode="ProgressBarMode.Indeterminate" Size="ProgressBarCircularSize.Medium" />
                <RadzenText Text="@Loc["Loading"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" />
            </RadzenStack>
        </RadzenCard>
    }

    @* ── Error state ── *@
    else if (_loadError is not null)
    {
        <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["ErrorTitle"]"
                     Text="@_loadError"
                     AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Danger"
                     Variant="Variant.Filled"
                     ShowIcon="true" />
    }

    @* ── Not found ── *@
    else if (_product is null)
    {
        <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["NotFoundTitle"]"
                     Text="@Loc["NotFoundMessage"]"
                     AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Warning"
                     Variant="Variant.Filled"
                     ShowIcon="true" />
    }

    @* ── Main content ── *@
    else
    {
        <div class="detail-grid">
            @* LEFT — picture (or placeholder) + staff-only "Change photo" button.
               Wrapped in .detail-picture-column so the photo-editor card (when
               open) stacks flush below the picture in the SAME grid cell —
               see the CSS comment on .detail-picture-column for why wrapping
               matters (otherwise the editor would land in row 2 of the grid,
               pushed down by the info column's height). *@
            <div class="detail-picture-column">
                <div class="detail-picture">
                    @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_product.PictureUrl))
                    {
                        <img src="@_product.PictureUrl" alt="@_product.Name" loading="lazy" />
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <RadzenIcon Icon="inventory_2" />
                    }

                    @* Staff-only "Change photo" overlay button — opens the same dropzone
                       UI used on CreateProduct.razor. Only rendered for staff (Admin /
                       Manager / Employee) — same role check as the rest of the staff
                       edit section below. *@
                    @if (_canEdit)
                    {
                        <div class="change-photo-overlay">
                            <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ChangePhoto"]"
                                          Icon="photo_camera"
                                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Secondary"
                                          Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                          Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                          Click="@(() => _isPhotoEditorOpen = true)" />
                        </div>
                    }
                </div>

                @* ── Photo editor (inline card under the picture) ──
                   Opens when staff clicks "Change Photo" on the picture above.
                   Rendered INSIDE the .detail-picture-column wrapper so it
                   stacks flush against the bottom of the picture (no gap from
                   the grid's row layout). Mirrors the CreateProduct.razor
                   picture dropzone + preview card UI. The user picks a file,
                   sees a preview, then clicks "Save photo" to:
                     1. Upload the new file via IFileStorage.SaveAsync.
                     2. Hard-delete the OLD file via IFileStorage.DeleteAsync.
                     3. Dispatch UpdateProductDetailsCommand with the new PictureUrl.
                   Cancel closes the editor without saving. Same validation rules
                   as CreateProduct: JPEG/PNG/WebP only, 5 MB max. *@
                @if (_isPhotoEditorOpen && _canEdit)
                {
                    <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 1.5rem; border-top: 2px solid var(--rz-primary);">
                        <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.5rem" Style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                            <RadzenIcon Icon="photo_camera" Style="color: var(--rz-primary);" />
                            <RadzenText Text="@Loc["ChangePhotoTitle"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.H6" Style="font-weight: 600; margin: 0;" />
                            <RadzenButton Icon="close"
                                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Light"
                                          Variant="Variant.Text"
                                          Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                          Style="margin-inline-start: auto;"
                                          Click="@(() => _isPhotoEditorOpen = false)"
                                          AriaLabel="@Loc["ClosePhotoEditor"]" />
                        </RadzenStack>

                        <div class="upload-section">
                            @if (_selectedFile is null)
                            {
                                <label class="picture-dropzone">
                                    <InputFile OnChange="@OnInputFileChange"
                                               accept="image/jpeg,image/png,image/webp"
                                               class="picture-dropzone-input" />
                                    <div class="picture-dropzone-body">
                                        <RadzenIcon Icon="cloud_upload"
                                                    Style="font-size: 2.5rem; color: var(--rz-primary);" />
                                        <div class="picture-dropzone-text">
                                            <span class="picture-dropzone-title">@Loc["UploadDropzoneTitle"]</span>
                                            <span class="picture-dropzone-hint">@Loc["UploadDropzoneHint"]</span>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </label>
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                <div class="upload-card">
                                    @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_previewDataUrl))
                                    {
                                        <img src="@_previewDataUrl" alt="preview" class="upload-preview" />
                                    }
                                    else
                                    {
                                        <div class="upload-preview-placeholder">
                                            <RadzenIcon Icon="image" />
                                        </div>
                                    }
                                    <div class="upload-info">
                                        <div class="file-name">@_selectedFile.Name</div>
                                        <div class="file-size">@FormatBytes(_selectedFile.Size)</div>
                                    </div>
                                    <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["RemoveImage"]"
                                                  Icon="delete"
                                                  ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Danger"
                                                  Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                                  Click="@RemoveSelectedImage" />
                                </div>
                                <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                            Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); display: block;">
                                    @Loc["PictureHint"]
                                </RadzenText>
                            }

                            @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_uploadError))
                            {
                                <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["UploadErrorTitle"]"
                                             Text="@_uploadError"
                                             AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Danger"
                                             Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                             ShowIcon="true" />
                            }

                            <div class="edit-actions">
                                <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["CancelPhotoEditor"]"
                                              Icon="close"
                                              ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Light"
                                              Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                              Disabled="@(_isSavingPhoto)"
                                              Click="@(() => _isPhotoEditorOpen = false)" />
                                <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["SavePhoto"]"
                                              Icon="save"
                                              ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                                              Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                              Disabled="@(_selectedFile is null || _selectedFileBytes is null || _isSavingPhoto)"
                                              Click="@HandleSavePhotoAsync" />
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </RadzenCard>
                }
            </div>

            @* RIGHT — info + purchase panel + staff-only edit section *@
            <div class="detail-info">
                @* Breadcrumb: Products → [Category Name] → [Product Name] *@
                <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="breadcrumb">
                    <a href="/Products">@Loc["BreadcrumbProducts"]</a>
                    @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_categoryHierarchy))
                    {
                        <span class="crumb-sep">/</span>
                        <span>@_categoryHierarchy</span>
                    }
                    <span class="crumb-sep">/</span>
                    <span class="crumb-current">@_product.Name</span>
                </nav>

                @* Product name *@
                <h1 class="detail-name">@_product.Name</h1>

                @* Price *@
                <div class="detail-price">@FormatPrice(_product.Price)</div>

                @* Description *@
                @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_product.Description))
                {
                    <p class="detail-description">@_product.Description</p>
                }

                @* Category hierarchy chip — shown to everyone (customer + staff).
                   Displays Category › SubCategory › SubSubCategory as a small
                   inline label so the customer can verify the categorization
                   without leaving the page. *@
                @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_categoryHierarchy))
                {
                    <div class="category-hierarchy">
                        <RadzenIcon Icon="category" Style="font-size: 1rem;" />
                        <span>@_categoryHierarchy</span>
                    </div>
                }

                @* The "Add to cart" purchase row was REMOVED per the user's
                   request — the product detail page is now a VIEW + STAFF
                   STOCK-MANAGEMENT surface. Customers still see the read-only
                   product info above (picture, name, price, description,
                   category hierarchy); staff additionally see the edit +
                   stock-set + per-group-limits sections below. Cart actions
                   happen via the customer-facing Products grid (/Products),
                   which still has its own Add-to-cart card UI. *@

                @* ── STAFF EDIT SECTION ──
                   Only shown to Admin / Manager / Employee. Contains:
                     1. Inline edit of Name + Description with Save button.
                     2. Per-group purchase limits editor.
                   The photo editor opens as a separate modal-like card above
                   (controlled by _isPhotoEditorOpen). All edits dispatch
                   Wolverine commands; the backend [RequireRoles] attribute
                   is the authoritative gate — the UI check just hides the
                   affordance for non-staff. *@
                @if (_canEdit)
                {
                    <div class="staff-section">
                        <div class="staff-section-title">
                            <RadzenIcon Icon="edit" />
                            <span>@Loc["StaffEditTitle"]</span>
                        </div>

                        @* Inline edit: Name + Description + Save button.
                           Editable copies are held in _editName / _editDescription
                           so the user can type freely without committing on each
                           keystroke. Save dispatches UpdateProductDetailsCommand
                           with the new values + the EXISTING picture URL + price
                           (we don't touch those here). *@
                        <div class="edit-row">
                            <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldName"]" Style="width: 100%;">
                                <RadzenTextBox @bind-Value="_editName"
                                               TValue="string"
                                               Style="width: 100%;" />
                            </RadzenFormField>
                        </div>
                        <div class="edit-row">
                            <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldDescription"]" Style="width: 100%;">
                                <RadzenTextArea @bind-Value="_editDescription"
                                                TValue="string"
                                                Rows="3"
                                                Style="width: 100%;" />
                            </RadzenFormField>
                        </div>
                        <div class="edit-actions">
                            <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["SaveDetails"]"
                                          Icon="save"
                                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                                          Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                          Disabled="@(_isSavingDetails || string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_editName))"
                                          Click="@HandleSaveDetailsAsync" />
                        </div>

                        @* ── Price editor section ──
                           Lets staff change the product's price. Uses a STRING-bound
                           RadzenTextBox (not RadzenNumeric) so we can format it ourselves:
                           thousands separators + Persian digits + 0 decimals for IRR.
                           Mirrors the salary-amount pattern on EditGroup.razor.

                           The currency is LOCKED (shown as a read-only pill) — changing
                           currency would invalidate already-purchased products priced in
                           the old currency. To use a different currency, the product must
                           be deactivated and a new one created.

                           On Save, dispatches UpdateProductDetailsCommand with the new
                           price + the EXISTING name/description/picture (we don't touch
                           those here). *@
                        <div class="staff-section-title" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
                            <RadzenIcon Icon="sell" />
                            <span>@Loc["PriceEditorTitle"]</span>
                        </div>

                        @* Current price display — read-only, for reference.
                           Uses FormatMoneyRial (NOT FormatPrice/FormatMoneyToman) because
                           the price textbox below expects the user to enter the amount in
                           RIAL (the raw DB amount). The top-of-page price display uses
                           Toman (÷10) for customer-facing readability, but here we need the
                           staff member to see the SAME unit they'll be typing. *@
                        <div style="border: 1px solid var(--rz-base-border-color);
                            border-left: 4px solid var(--rz-primary);
                            border-radius: var(--tm-radius, 0);
                            padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
                            background: var(--rz-component-background-color, var(--rz-base-background-color));
                            margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                            <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.5rem">
                                <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption" Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);">
                                    @Loc["PriceCurrentLabel"]
                                </RadzenText>
                                <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Subtitle1" Style="font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;">
                                    @CultureFormat.FormatMoneyRial(_product.Price)
                                </RadzenText>
                            </RadzenStack>
                        </div>

                        <div class="edit-row">
                            <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["PriceNewLabel"]" Style="width: 100%;">
                                <RadzenTextBox @bind-Value="_editPriceText"
                                               TValue="string"
                                               Style="width: 100%; direction: ltr; text-align: left;"
                                               Placeholder="@Loc["PriceNewPlaceholder"]"
                                               @onfocus="OnEditPriceFocus"
                                               @onblur="OnEditPriceBlur" />
                            </RadzenFormField>
                            <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                        Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);">
                                @Loc["PriceHint"]
                            </RadzenText>
                        </div>
                        <div class="edit-actions">
                            <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["SavePrice"]"
                                          Icon="save"
                                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                                          Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                          Disabled="@(_isSavingPrice)"
                                          Click="@HandleSavePriceAsync" />
                        </div>

                        @* ── Category editor section ──
                           Lets staff reassign the product to a different Category /
                           SubCategory / SubSubCategory. Only EXISTING (active)
                           categories are offered — there's no "create new" affordance
                           here; categories are managed on /Admin/Categories.

                           The three dropdowns cascade: picking a Category filters
                           the SubCategory dropdown to that Category's children,
                           picking a SubCategory filters the SubSubCategory dropdown.
                           Switching Category clears Sub + SubSub; switching Sub
                           clears SubSub. Same UX as CreateProduct.razor.

                           On Save, dispatches UpdateProductCategoryCommand — the
                           handler validates the hierarchy server-side and the
                           domain enforces "SubSub requires Sub" (so the UI can't
                           leave the aggregate in an inconsistent state). The
                           command requires Employee / Manager / Admin, matching
                           the page's _canEdit gate (same role set). *@
                        <div class="staff-section-title" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
                            <RadzenIcon Icon="category" />
                            <span>@Loc["CategoryEditorTitle"]</span>
                        </div>

                        @if (_isLoadingCategories)
                        {
                            <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body2"
                                        Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);">
                                @Loc["CategoryEditorLoading"]
                            </RadzenText>
                        }
                        else if (_categories.Count == 0)
                        {
                            <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body2"
                                        Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);">
                                @Loc["CategoryEditorEmpty"]
                            </RadzenText>
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <div class="category-row">
                                <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldCategory"]" Style="width: 100%;">
                                    <RadzenDropDown TValue="Guid?"
                                                    Value="_editCategoryId"
                                                    Data="_categories"
                                                    TextProperty="Name"
                                                    ValueProperty="Id"
                                                    Placeholder="@Loc["CategoryPlaceholder"]"
                                                    ValueChanged="@OnEditCategoryChanged"
                                                    Disabled="@_isSavingCategory"
                                                    Style="width: 100%;" />
                                </RadzenFormField>

                                <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldSubCategory"]" Style="width: 100%;">
                                    <RadzenDropDown TValue="Guid?"
                                                    Value="_editSubCategoryId"
                                                    Data="_availableSubCategories"
                                                    TextProperty="Name"
                                                    ValueProperty="Id"
                                                    AllowClear="true"
                                                    Placeholder="@Loc["CategoryOptionalPlaceholder"]"
                                                    ValueChanged="@OnEditSubCategoryChanged"
                                                    Disabled="@(_isSavingCategory || _editCategoryId == null)"
                                                    Style="width: 100%;" />
                                </RadzenFormField>

                                <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldSubSubCategory"]" Style="width: 100%;">
                                    <RadzenDropDown TValue="Guid?"
                                                    Value="_editSubSubCategoryId"
                                                    Data="_availableSubSubCategories"
                                                    TextProperty="Name"
                                                    ValueProperty="Id"
                                                    AllowClear="true"
                                                    Placeholder="@Loc["CategoryOptionalPlaceholder"]"
                                                    Disabled="@(_isSavingCategory || _editSubCategoryId == null)"
                                                    Style="width: 100%;" />
                                </RadzenFormField>
                            </div>

                            <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                        Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); display: block; margin-top: 0.25rem;">
                                @Loc["CategoryEditorHint"]
                            </RadzenText>

                            <div class="edit-actions">
                                <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["SaveCategory"]"
                                              Icon="save"
                                              ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                                              Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                              Disabled="@(_isSavingCategory || _editCategoryId == null)"
                                              Click="@HandleSaveCategoryAsync" />
                            </div>
                        }

                        @* ── Stock-set section ──
                           Lets staff set the product's stock to an EXACT value
                           (not additive). Dispatches SetProductStockCommand,
                           which calls Product.AdjustStockTo — the domain enforces
                           quantity > 0 (zero and negatives are rejected with a
                           clear message telling the user to use the Deactivate
                           action instead).

                           WHY A SEPARATE SECTION (not just a button on the
                           AdminProducts grid):
                             The grid's Restock action ADDS to stock (delta =
                             +N). The user wanted a way to set stock to an
                           absolute value (stock = N), e.g. after a stock-take
                           when they know the actual physical count. Putting
                           it on the detail page keeps the grid uncluttered
                           and gives staff a clear "current value + new value"
                           side-by-side view. *@
                        <div class="staff-section-title" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
                            <RadzenIcon Icon="inventory_2" />
                            <span>@Loc["StockSetTitle"]</span>
                        </div>

                        @* Current stock display — read-only boxed value, mirroring
                           the RestockProductDialog's current-stock box. *@
                        <div style="border: 1px solid var(--rz-base-border-color);
                            border-left: 4px solid var(--rz-primary);
                            border-radius: var(--tm-radius, 0);
                            padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
                            background: var(--rz-component-background-color, var(--rz-base-background-color));
                            margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                            <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.5rem">
                                <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption" Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);">
                                    @Loc["StockSetCurrentLabel"]
                                </RadzenText>
                                <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Subtitle1" Style="font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;">
                                    @(CultureFormat.FormatNumber(_product.StockQuantity))
                                </RadzenText>
                            </RadzenStack>
                        </div>

                        @* New stock value input — native <input type="number"> with
                           dir="ltr" to avoid RadzenNumeric's RTL caret bug (see the
                           qty-input comment that used to live above for the long
                           explanation). min="1" enforces positivity at the HTML
                           level. The validator + domain guard enforce it server-side. *@
                        <div class="edit-row">
                            <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["StockSetNewLabel"]" Style="width: 100%;">
                                <input type="number"
                                       class="rz-textbox"
                                       dir="ltr"
                                       step="1"
                                       min="1"
                                       placeholder="@Loc["StockSetPlaceholder"]"
                                       @bind="_editStock"
                                       @bind:culture="CultureInfo.CurrentCulture"
                                       style="width: 100%; text-align: left;" />
                            </RadzenFormField>
                            <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                        Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);">
                                @Loc["StockSetHint"]
                            </RadzenText>
                            @if (_showStockError)
                            {
                                <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption" Style="color: var(--rz-danger);">
                                    @Loc["StockSetRequiredError"]
                                </RadzenText>
                            }
                        </div>
                        <div class="edit-actions">
                            <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["StockSetButton"]"
                                          Icon="save"
                                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                                          Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                          Disabled="@(_isSavingStock)"
                                          Click="@HandleSetStockAsync" />
                        </div>

                        @* ── Per-group purchase limits editor ──
                           Shows ALL existing group names with their current
                           limits (or an empty input if no limit is set).
                           Each row has:
                             - Group name (read-only)
                             - Limit input (RadzenNumeric, min=1, max=1_000_000)
                             - "Save" button → SetProductPurchaseLimitCommand
                             - "Remove" button (only when a limit exists) →
                               RemoveProductPurchaseLimitCommand
                           Plus an "Add custom group" button below for groups
                           that don't exist yet (forward-looking). *@
                        <div class="staff-section-title" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
                            <RadzenIcon Icon="rule" />
                            <span>@Loc["PurchaseLimitsTitle"]</span>
                        </div>
                        <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                    Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
                            @Loc["PurchaseLimitsHint"]
                        </RadzenText>

                        @if (_isLoadingGroups)
                        {
                            <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body2"
                                        Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);">
                                @Loc["LoadingGroups"]
                            </RadzenText>
                        }
                        else if (_limitRows.Count == 0)
                        {
                            <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body2"
                                        Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);">
                                @Loc["NoLimitRows"]
                            </RadzenText>
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            @foreach (var row in _limitRows)
                            {
                                <div class="limit-row">
                                    <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldLimitGroup"]"
                                                     Style="flex: 1 1 200px; min-width: 160px;">
                                        @* SALARY FEATURE (Step 8): all rows are existing-group
                                           rows now (no more "Add custom group name" flow).
                                           The group NAME is read-only display; only the limit
                                           is editable. The GroupId is what gets passed to the
                                           Set/Remove command. *@
                                        <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1"
                                                    Style="display: block; padding: 0.5rem 0; font-weight: 600;">
                                            @row.GroupName
                                        </RadzenText>
                                    </RadzenFormField>
                                    <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldLimitValue"]"
                                                     Style="flex: 0 1 140px; min-width: 100px;">
                                        @* Same RTL-caret fix as the qty-input above —
                                           native <input type="number"> with dir="ltr"
                                           bypasses RadzenNumeric's JS, which mishandles
                                           caret position in fa-IR mode. row.Limit is int?,
                                           so an empty input binds back to null correctly. *@
                                        <input type="number"
                                               class="rz-textbox"
                                               dir="ltr"
                                               step="1"
                                               min="1"
                                               max="1000000"
                                               placeholder="@Loc["LimitValuePlaceholder"]"
                                               @bind="row.Limit"
                                               @bind:culture="CultureInfo.CurrentCulture"
                                               style="width: 100%; text-align: left;" />
                                    </RadzenFormField>
                                    <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["SaveLimit"]"
                                                  Icon="save"
                                                  ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                                                  Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                                  Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                                  Disabled="@(!row.Limit.HasValue || row.GroupId == Guid.Empty || row.IsSaving)"
                                                  Click="@(() => HandleSaveLimitAsync(row))" />
                                    <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["RemoveLimit"]"
                                                  Icon="delete"
                                                  ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Danger"
                                                  Variant="Variant.Text"
                                                  Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                                  Disabled="@(!row.HasExistingLimit || row.IsSaving)"
                                                  Click="@(() => HandleRemoveLimitAsync(row))" />
                                </div>
                            }
                        }

                        @* SALARY FEATURE (Step 8): the "Add custom group" button is gone —
                           admins must create groups via the CreateGroup page first.
                           When no existing groups are present, the empty-state message
                           shows a link to /Admin/Groups/Create. *@
                        @if (!_isLoadingGroups && _limitRows.Count == 0)
                        {
                            <div style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">
                                <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ActionCreateGroup"]"
                                              Icon="group_add"
                                              ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Secondary"
                                              Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                              Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                              Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/Admin/Groups/Create", forceLoad: false))" />
                            </div>
                        }
                    </div>
                }
            </div>
        </div>
    }
</RadzenStack>

@code {
    // ── Route parameter ────────────────────────────────────────────────

    [Parameter]
    public Guid Id { get; set; }

    // ── State ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private ProductDto? _product;
    private string? _categoryHierarchy;
    private string? _loadError;
    private bool _isLoading = true;

    /// <summary>
    /// True if the current user is in Admin/Manager/Employee role. Computed
    /// once in OnInitializedAsync via AuthenticationStateProvider (NOT
    /// ICurrentUserService.IsInRole — see the file header for why).
    /// Gates the entire staff-edit section + the Change Photo button + the
    /// role-aware Back button label/destination.
    /// </summary>
    private bool _canEdit;

    // ── Editable copies for the Name/Description inline editor ──

    private string _editName = string.Empty;
    private string _editDescription = string.Empty;
    private bool _isSavingDetails;

    // ── Price editor state (staff-only) ──
    //
    // Holds the user's input for the "Change price" field. Mirrors the
    // salary-amount pattern on EditGroup.razor / CreateGroup.razor — we
    // bind a STRING (not a decimal) so we can format it ourselves
    // (thousands separators + Persian digits + 0 decimals for IRR).
    // See EditGroup.razor for the full rationale.

    private string _editPriceText = string.Empty;
    private bool _isSavingPrice;

    // ── Stock-set editor state (staff-only) ──
    //
    // Holds the user's input for the "Set stock" field. Null = empty (no
    // value entered yet). The min=1 on the input + the SetProductStockCommand
    // validator + Product.AdjustStockTo domain guard all enforce > 0.

    private int? _editStock;
    private bool _isSavingStock;
    private bool _showStockError;

    // ── Category editor state (staff-only) ──
    //
    // Holds the user's selections for the three-level category cascade.
    // _editCategoryId is required (every product must belong to a Category);
    // _editSubCategoryId / _editSubSubCategoryId are nullable (a product can
    // live at the Category level only, or at the Category/Sub level only).
    //
    // The cascade is identical to CreateProduct's category picker:
    //   - _categories            → ALL active categories (loaded once)
    //   - _availableSubCategories → filtered to the selected Category's children
    //   - _availableSubSubCategories → filtered to the selected SubCategory's children
    // Switching the Category resets Sub + SubSub; switching Sub resets SubSub.

    private List<CategoryDto> _categories = new();
    private List<SubCategoryDto> _availableSubCategories = new();
    private List<SubSubCategoryDto> _availableSubSubCategories = new();
    private Guid? _editCategoryId;
    private Guid? _editSubCategoryId;
    private Guid? _editSubSubCategoryId;
    private bool _isLoadingCategories;
    private bool _isSavingCategory;

    // ── Photo editor state ──
    //
    // Mirrors CreateProduct.razor's pattern. The file is buffered in
    // memory immediately in OnInputFileChange (NOT at submit time) to
    // avoid the JSException that occurs when the JS-side _blazorFilesById
    // registry is cleared by Hot Reload / circuit reconnect / runtime
    // housekeeping.

    private bool _isPhotoEditorOpen;
    private IBrowserFile? _selectedFile;
    private byte[]? _selectedFileBytes;
    private string? _previewDataUrl;
    private string? _uploadError;
    private bool _isSavingPhoto;

    private const long MaxFileSize = 5 * 1024 * 1024; // 5 MB

    private static readonly HashSet<string> AllowedContentTypes = new(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
    {
        "image/jpeg", "image/png", "image/webp"
    };

    // ── Purchase-limit editor state ──

    /// <summary>
    /// One row per group. Loaded once on page init
    /// by combining GetAllCustomerGroupsQuery (every existing group) with
    /// the product's existing limits (so each row shows its current
    /// value, or an empty input if no limit is set yet).
    /// </summary>
    private List<LimitRow> _limitRows = new();
    private bool _isLoadingGroups = true;

    /// <summary>
    /// One row in the per-group purchase-limit editor. Each row maps to
    /// either a SetProductPurchaseLimitCommand (when "Save" is clicked
    /// with a non-empty limit) or a RemoveProductPurchaseLimitCommand
    /// (when "Remove" is clicked — only available for rows that currently
    /// have a limit).
    ///
    /// SALARY FEATURE (Step 8): the row now carries GroupId (Guid FK) and
    /// GroupName (display-only string). The "Add custom group name" flow
    /// is gone — admins must create groups via the CreateGroup page first,
    /// so every limit row references a real CustomerGroup row.
    /// </summary>
    private sealed class LimitRow
    {
        /// <summary>
        /// The customer group Id this limit applies to. Set once at row
        /// creation (from CustomerGroupListItemDto.Id or
        /// ProductPurchaseLimitDto.GroupId). Never mutated by the UI.
        /// </summary>
        public Guid GroupId { get; init; }

        /// <summary>
        /// The customer group's DISPLAY NAME (read from the source DTO).
        /// Used only for rendering — never passed to the command.
        /// </summary>
        public string GroupName { get; init; } = string.Empty;

        public int? Limit { get; set; }

        /// <summary>
        /// True if this group currently has a limit set on this product
        /// (loaded from _product.PurchaseLimits at init time). Drives the
        /// enabled state of the "Remove" button.
        /// </summary>
        public bool HasExistingLimit { get; set; }

        /// <summary>
        /// True while a Save or Remove command is in flight for this row.
        /// Disables both buttons to prevent double-clicks.
        /// </summary>
        public bool IsSaving { get; set; }
    }

    // ── Lifecycle ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        // Resolve role + (if staff) limit-editor data alongside the product
        // load. All three are independent reads.
        try
        {
            await ResolveRoleAsync();
            await LoadProductAsync();

            // After product loads, fire the category lookup + (for staff)
            // the group-names lookup in parallel.
            if (_product is not null)
            {
                _editName = _product.Name;
                _editDescription = _product.Description;

                // Seed the price-editor textbox with the product's current
                // price (formatted with thousands separators + Persian digits
                // in fa-IR mode + 0 decimals for IRR — see FormatPriceForDisplay).
                _editPriceText = FormatPriceForDisplay(_product.Price.Amount, _product.Price.Currency);

                // Seed the category-editor cascade with the product's current
                // assignment so the dropdowns open showing the current
                // Category / SubCategory / SubSubCategory instead of blanks.
                _editCategoryId = _product.CategoryId;
                _editSubCategoryId = _product.SubCategoryId;
                _editSubSubCategoryId = _product.SubSubCategoryId;

                var categoryTask = LoadCategoryHierarchyAsync();
                var groupsTask = _canEdit ? LoadGroupNamesAsync() : Task.CompletedTask;
                var categoriesTask = _canEdit ? LoadCategoriesAsync() : Task.CompletedTask;
                await Task.WhenAll(categoryTask, groupsTask, categoriesTask);
            }
        }
        finally
        {
            _isLoading = false;
        }
    }

    private async Task ResolveRoleAsync()
    {
        try
        {
            var authState = await AuthStateProvider.GetAuthenticationStateAsync();
            var user = authState.User;
            _canEdit = user.IsInRole(Roles.Admin)
                       || user.IsInRole(Roles.Manager)
                       || user.IsInRole(Roles.Employee);
        }
        catch
        {
            // Safe fallback — if role resolution fails, treat as non-staff.
            // The backend handlers ALSO enforce [RequireRoles] as
            // defense-in-depth, so even if a non-staff user could see the
            // buttons, the dispatch would be rejected.
            _canEdit = false;
        }
    }

    // ── Data loading ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private async Task LoadProductAsync()
    {
        var query = new GetProductByIdQuery { ProductId = Id };
        var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result<ProductDto>>(query);

        if (result.IsSuccess)
        {
            _product = result.Value;
        }
        else
        {
            _loadError = result.Error ?? Loc["Error_GenericLoad"];
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Loads the full category hierarchy (Category › SubCategory › SubSubCategory)
    /// for the product's CategoryId. Non-fatal — if the lookup fails, the
    /// breadcrumb just shows "Products / [Product]" without the category.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task LoadCategoryHierarchyAsync()
    {
        if (_product is null || _product.CategoryId == Guid.Empty)
        {
            return;
        }

        try
        {
            var query = new GetCategoryByIdWithHierarchyQuery { CategoryId = _product.CategoryId };
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result<CategoryDto>>(query);

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                var cat = result.Value;
                var parts = new List<string> { cat.Name };

                if (_product.SubCategoryId.HasValue)
                {
                    var sub = cat.SubCategories.FirstOrDefault(s => s.Id == _product.SubCategoryId.Value);
                    if (sub is not null)
                    {
                        parts.Add(sub.Name);

                        if (_product.SubSubCategoryId.HasValue)
                        {
                            var subsub = sub.SubSubCategories.FirstOrDefault(ss => ss.Id == _product.SubSubCategoryId.Value);
                            if (subsub is not null)
                            {
                                parts.Add(subsub.Name);
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }

                _categoryHierarchy = string.Join(" › ", parts);
            }
            // Non-fatal.
        }
        catch
        {
            // Swallow — breadcrumb is purely a UI nicety.
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Loads the active category tree for the staff-only category editor.
    /// Populates _categories (all active Categories) and — if the product
    /// currently has a Category / SubCategory selected — also populates
    /// _availableSubCategories / _availableSubSubCategories so the dropdowns
    /// show the right child options on first render (otherwise the Sub
    /// dropdown would be empty until the user re-picks the Category).
    ///
    /// Non-fatal: if the load fails, the editor just shows an empty list
    /// and the user can't change the category until they refresh.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task LoadCategoriesAsync()
    {
        _isLoadingCategories = true;
        try
        {
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result<List<CategoryDto>>>(
                new GetActiveCategoriesQuery());

            if (result.IsSuccess && result.Value is not null)
            {
                _categories = result.Value;

                // If the product currently has a CategoryId, seed the Sub
                // dropdown's available options from that Category's children
                // so the user sees the current SubCategory pre-selected on
                // first render (rather than the dropdown being empty until
                // they re-pick the Category).
                if (_editCategoryId is not null
                    && _categories.FirstOrDefault(c => c.Id == _editCategoryId.Value) is { } currentCat)
                {
                    _availableSubCategories = currentCat.SubCategories;

                    // Same for SubSub: if a Sub is selected, find its parent
                    // SubCategory and seed the SubSub dropdown from its children.
                    if (_editSubCategoryId is not null
                        && _availableSubCategories.FirstOrDefault(sc => sc.Id == _editSubCategoryId.Value) is { } currentSub)
                    {
                        _availableSubSubCategories = currentSub.SubSubCategories;
                    }
                }
            }
            // Non-fatal — editor shows empty list on failure.
        }
        catch
        {
            // Swallow — the category editor will just show empty dropdowns.
        }
        finally
        {
            _isLoadingCategories = false;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Loads all active customer groups + seeds one LimitRow per group.
    /// For each row that matches an existing limit on this product,
    /// pre-populates the Limit + sets HasExistingLimit so the Remove
    /// button is enabled. Also seeds rows for any existing limit whose
    /// GroupId doesn't appear in the GetAllCustomerGroupsQuery result
    /// (e.g. the group was deactivated but the limit remains — the row
    /// is shown so the admin can remove the stale limit).
    /// </summary>
    private async Task LoadGroupNamesAsync()
    {
        _isLoadingGroups = true;
        try
        {
            // Include inactive groups so we can surface stale limit rows
            // (limits set for a group that was later deactivated). The
            // admin can then remove the stale limit.
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result<List<CustomerGroupListItemDto>>>(
                new GetAllCustomerGroupsQuery { IncludeInactive = true });

            var groups = (result.IsSuccess && result.Value is not null)
                ? result.Value
                : new List<CustomerGroupListItemDto>();

            // Build a lookup of existing limits on this product for quick
            // matching by GroupId.
            var existingLimits = _product?.PurchaseLimits ?? new List<ProductPurchaseLimitDto>();
            var existingByGroupId = existingLimits
                .Where(l => l.GroupId != Guid.Empty)
                .ToDictionary(l => l.GroupId, l => l.Limit);

            var seenGroupIds = new HashSet<Guid>();

            // Seed one row per existing group (active OR inactive — see
            // IncludeInactive=true above).
            foreach (var group in groups.OrderBy(g => g.Name, StringComparer.CurrentCulture))
            {
                var hasLimit = existingByGroupId.TryGetValue(group.Id, out var limit);
                _limitRows.Add(new LimitRow
                {
                    GroupId = group.Id,
                    GroupName = group.Name,
                    Limit = hasLimit ? limit : null,
                    HasExistingLimit = hasLimit
                });
                seenGroupIds.Add(group.Id);
            }

            // Defensive: surface any existing limit whose GroupId doesn't
            // match a row in GetAllCustomerGroupsQuery's result. This
            // shouldn't happen (groups are soft-deleted, not hard-deleted),
            // but if it does, the admin can remove the orphan limit.
            foreach (var limit in existingLimits)
            {
                if (!seenGroupIds.Contains(limit.GroupId))
                {
                    _limitRows.Add(new LimitRow
                    {
                        GroupId = limit.GroupId,
                        GroupName = limit.GroupName ?? "(unknown group)",
                        Limit = limit.Limit,
                        HasExistingLimit = true
                    });
                }
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            // Silent failure — the limits editor just shows empty.
        }
        finally
        {
            _isLoadingGroups = false;
        }
    }

